post.description:
Store a channel. A webhook channel's response carries its signing `secret`, once.

`409 NOT_CONFIGURED` for Slack, webhook and PagerDuty without CREDENTIALS_KEYS;
`409 CHANNEL_NAME_TAKEN`; `422 LIMIT_EXCEEDED` past 20 channels; `422 RECIPIENT_NOT_MEMBER`;
`422 UNSAFE_URL` for a webhook URL that is not `https://` or resolves to a private address.

Save the route as version 1. The project's first route becomes its default.

`422` on `config.targets.<i>.credential_id` for a credential that is not the organization's;
`409 ROUTE_NAME_TAKEN` for a name already used in the project.

Add the next version. `409 KIND_MISMATCH` when the kind differs from the prompt's;
`409 NO_CHANGES` when nothing differs from the latest version; `429 RATE_LIMITED` after 100
versions of the prompt in a UTC day (`Retry-After` is the time to midnight).
